      proofName: "Translation to the kernel",
      formula: String.raw`\varphi \text{ injective} \iff \ker \varphi = \{e\}`,
      text: "A group homomorphism is injective exactly when its kernel consists of the neutral element only.",
      proof: "φ(a) = φ(b) holds exactly when φ(a<sup>−1</sup>b) = e, using φ(a<sup>−1</sup>) = φ(a)<sup>−1</sup>.",
